# Two ways a reachability check used to test a port some other program answers,
# and so report it "occupied". a starts in automatic mode on 1411, which x on the
# same host holds: a must neither map nor measure a port it did not bind. Moved
# to 4111 with UPnP, a asks for a port c's mapping already has, and the gateway
# grants another: the check must test the granted port, not 4111 (which is c).

preset application Network Bind6 ""
@x preset application Network Mode advanced
@x preset application Network Port 1411
@c preset application Network Mode advanced
@c preset application Network Bind 0.0.0.0
@c preset application Network Port 4111
@c preset application Network "Active mode" 1
@c preset application Network UseUPnP 1
@c preset application Network "Reachability server" ${DROP}
@a preset application Network "Reachability server" ${DROP}

@c wait ReachabilityMeasured verdict.tcp=open verdict.udp=open verdict.port=4111 timeout=30s
@a wait CoreStatus port=0
@a measure
@a wait ReachabilityCheckFailed why=CheckFailed reason="IPv4: there is no peer port to test" timeout=30s

@a set application Network Port 4111
@a wait CoreStatus port=4111 timeout=10s
@a set application Network UseUPnP 1
@a set application Network "Active mode" 1
@a set application Network Mode advanced
@a wait ReachabilityMeasured verdict.tcp=open verdict.udp=open verdict.port!=4111 remember EXTERNAL=verdict.port timeout=30s
@a measure
@a wait ReachabilityMeasured verdict.tcp=open verdict.udp=open verdict.port=$EXTERNAL timeout=30s
@a expect-no ReachabilityMeasured verdict.tcp=occupied
